    "id": "p24-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Show, using substitution, that $E(-12,-5)$ lies on the circle centred at the origin with radius 13.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-12)^2+(-5)^2=144+25=169=13^2$, so $E$ lies on the circle.",
      "worked": "The circle has equation $x^2+y^2=169$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(-12)^2+(-5)^2&=144+25\\\\(-12)^2+(-5)^2&=169\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $E$ lies on the circle.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
